use std
into noise_test.amni

A test program for the `noise` library; imports math, vec, os and noise.noise. Already provided and never defined here, in namespace noise: the kind constants `VALUE`, `PERLIN`, `SIMPLEX`, `CELL_F1`, `CELL_F2`, `CELL_EDGE` and `CELL_VALUE`; the fractal constants `NONE`, `FBM`, `RIDGED` and `BILLOW`; `GOLDEN64`; `mix64(v u64) u64`, `unit_of(h u64) real`, `perlin3(seed u64, p double3) real`, `cell_point(seed u64, cx int, cy int, cz int) double3, u64`, `base(kind int, seed u64, p double3) real`; the struct `Noise` (fields kind, seed, step, frequency, fractal, octaves, lacunarity, gain, warp, warp_freq) and `make(kind int, seed int) Noise`; `layered(n, p) real`, `sample(n, p) real` and `fill2(n, x0, z0, y, step, w, h, out)` (out a growable f32 list). From os, `time_ns()`. A counter `FAILS`; `check(ok, label, detail)` prints "ok " or "FAIL ", the label, a space and the detail, and counts failures. `r4(x)` rounds to four decimals for printing. `NAMES` lists the kind names "value", "perlin", "simplex", "cell_f1", "cell_f2", "cell_edge" and "cell_value" by kind number.

A random point source: module variable `RS u64`; `reset(s int)` sets RS to s as u64; `rnd() real` adds GOLDEN64 to RS and gives `unit_of(mix64(RS))`; `point() double3` is three `rnd()` each mapped to [-50, 50] (100 times it minus 50); `dir() double3` is a random unit vector (three values 2 rnd() minus 1, normalized; draw again when its length is below 0.01).

`n1_n2()`: for each kind 0 to 6: reset(7), n = make(kind, 7); over 100,000 points v = `sample(n, point())`: count values outside [-1, 1], add up v and v squared. Mean and standard deviation (population). Print the kind's name, mean and standard deviation. Also for perlin, over the same 100,000 points again (reset(7)), count raw `perlin3(7, p)` values outside [-1, 1] and track the largest absolute value. Check "N1 every sample in [-1, 1]" over all kinds with the total count outside; check "N1 raw perlin rarely clamps" when its outside count is below 100, detail the count and the largest. Check "N2 value, perlin and simplex balanced" when for those three the absolute mean is below 0.05 and the deviation is from 0.1 to 0.6, detail each mean and deviation; check "N2 cellular kinds vary" when the four cellular kinds each have deviation above 0.1.

`n3()`: for each kind: reset(11); over 100,000 points p, q = p plus `dir()` times 1e-5; the largest absolute difference of `sample` at p and q with make(kind, 7). Check "N3 continuous" when that is below 1e-3 for every kind but CELL_VALUE, detail the largest of them; check "N3 control: cell value jumps" when CELL_VALUE's is above 0.1.

`n4()`: for each kind: reset(13), with a = make(kind, 7) and b = make(kind, 7), count points of 10,000 where `sample` of a and of b differ at all, and for seeds 1 and 2 the Pearson correlation of `sample` over those 10,000 points (0 when either spread is 0). Check "N4 same seed, same values" when no point differs; check "N4 seeds independent" when every kind's absolute correlation is below 0.05, detail the largest.

`n6()`: reset(17); over 20,000 points p with c the floor of each component as ints, brute force: for every cell with offsets -3 to 3 on each axis, its point q from `cell_point(7, cell)`, d = the squared length of q minus p; keep the smallest b1 and second smallest b2; the same over offsets -1 to 1 only gives s2. Expected values: e1 = 2 times the square root of b1 minus 1, e2 = the square root of b2 minus 1, each clamped to [-1, 1]. Count points where the absolute difference of `base(CELL_F1, 7, p)` and e1, or of `base(CELL_F2, 7, p)` and e2, is above 1e-12; count points where s2 is not equal to b2. Check "N6 cellular F1 and F2 exact" when the first count is 0; check "N6 control: a 3x3x3 search misses some" when the second is above 0, detail both counts.

`n7()`: for fractals FBM, RIDGED and BILLOW with kind PERLIN, seed 7 and 5 octaves, reset(19), count `sample` values over 100,000 points outside [-1, 1]; check "N7 fractals in [-1, 1]" when the total is 0. Detail: `rough(oct) real` with n = make(PERLIN, 7), fractal FBM and that many octaves: reset(23), over 10,000 points the mean absolute difference of `sample` at p and at p plus `dir()` times 0.01, divided by the standard deviation of `sample` at those 10,000 points p. ratio = rough(5) over rough(1); check "N7 octaves add detail" when ratio is at least 1.5; print both roughnesses and ratio.

`n8()`: n = make(PERLIN, 7) with fractal FBM and 3 octaves; reset(29): over 10,000 points, with n.warp 0 count points where `sample(n, p)` is not exactly equal to `layered(n, p)` clamped to [-1, 1]; with m a copy of n with warp 1, the mean absolute difference of `sample(m, p)` and `sample(n, p)`. Check "N8 no warp, same field" when the count is 0; check "N8 warp moves values" when the mean is above 0.05, detail it.

`n9()`: n = make(PERLIN, 7) with fractal FBM, 5 octaves and frequency 1/64; a fresh f32 list; time `fill2(n, 0, 0, 0.37, 1, 512, 512, out)` with `time_ns`; check "N9 512x512 5-octave fBm" when it took under 150 ms and out has 262,144 values, detail milliseconds. Then for each kind, reset(31), time 100,000 `sample` calls of make(kind, 7) at `point()`, summing the values into a module real `SINK`; print the name and nanoseconds per sample.

`main()`: n1_n2, n3, n4, n6, n7, n8, n9; print "noise: ok", or "noise: FAILED " and the count and exit 1.
